{0 hermetic}

Enforce Eio's capabilities at compile time.

{!Hermetic} is a prelude that restates OCaml's standard library. In a file
that opens it, a standard library, [Unix] or [Thread] value that reaches the
file system, a clock, the network, the standard streams, entropy, a domain or
a child process on its own is a type error. This covers [Sys] too, so
[Sys.remove] and [Sys.command] are refused. Its alert names the [Eio.Stdenv] capability to take instead.
The unsafe operations that could forge a capability, such as [Obj.magic] or
a [Marshal] reader, are refused too. A source file opens the prelude on its
first line:

{[
open! Hermetic
]}

{1:api API}

{!modules: Hermetic}

{!Hermetic} is the prelude: the standard library, [Unix] and [Thread], with
each refused value given a type nothing consumes and an alert that says why.
The [Hermetic__] units it aliases hold the restated modules; a program names
them through {!Hermetic}, never directly.
